- op: discuss  # a1fe
  at: '2026-08-29T23:36:31Z'  # a1fe
  by: agent  # a1fe
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a1fe
  clock: 4  # a1fe
  nonce: a1fe  # a1fe
  message: "SHIPPED in PR #636. net_listen carries all three of ADR-0049 ruling 2's clauses; NO catalogue row uses it yet, so no shipped output changed. Schema 2.1 -> 2.2.\n\nTHE SCOPE CORRECTION HELD UP UNDER IMPLEMENTATION. This item said clause 3 was 'in OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES'; that set is TOTAL opacity and membership would have sent every server in every language to inconclusive on fs_write and env_read. The shadow is a boundary-keyed map instead (net_listen -> net_recv), which turned out to be EXISTING LAW rather than a new design: untyped_receiver_sites is keyed the same way, with a note recording that its unscoped form was measured on 2026-08-11 and marked DO NOT BUILD IT. 'net_listen not in OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES' is asserted as an ABSENCE, because a tidy that widened it would pass every opacity test in the tree.\n\nTWO MORE EMBEDDED LESSONS REUSED RATHER THAN RE-LEARNED. (1) Ask the CATALOGUE, not the returned boundary -- classify_call yields one primitive, so a row-order accident would otherwise decide whether a call defers; the registry parity test caught that shape on Scala for opacity. IoBoundaryCatalog.deferred_crossings() asks over every row. (2) The caveat goes in the ONE _clean_caveats builder, not at the four clean paths, which the module's own docstring names as its repeated failure.\n\nTHE REQUIRED EVIDENCE: ADR-0016's three-row table reproduced. With the shadow map emptied, the same edge and the same claim yield a BARE confirmed over a live listener, because a retagged call is still classified and still counts as examined (INV-buzab). That control is what makes clause 3 non-optional, and it is the test that fails first if anyone widens the shadow into OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES.\n\nA REAL DRIFT THE SCHEMA GATE CAUGHT: cmd_io_boundaries rebuilds the JSON envelope BY HAND on the filtered path, so net_listen_edges landed in one of two homes and the paths would have disagreed (INV-pubom). Fixed, plus a DERIVED gate -- every _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES member must have a <boundary>_edges key in both paths -- so the next bucket is covered on the commit that adds it rather than when someone remembers a hardcoded list.\n\nTWO CI ROUNDS, BOTH INSTRUCTIVE. Round 1 failed on COVERAGE, not correctness: my local --full reported 100% across 24745 tests while CI holds changed files to 100% under the narrower committed manifest, and two lines were only covered incidentally in the wide run. That is exactly the cross-package gap check-package-coverage exists to catch and I had not run it. verify_claims.py:672 was my own '+N more' truncation branch, untested because every fixture used one site. io_boundary.py:2390 is NOT my code and is UNREACHABLE FROM REAL DATA -- unruled_multi_boundary_primitives returns [] across all fifteen catalogues with and without overlays, so the 'visible debt' reporter has no debt; it became coverage-relevant only because this PR added a value to CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES. Building the synthetic fixture surfaced the predicate's real contract: boundary_ruling UNSET returns None, not 'unruled' -- 'nothing declared' and 'declared open' are different states, which is the INV-vaduk split that made multi_boundary_reason necessary. My first fixture assumed they were the same and failed correctly.\n\nRound 2's 'CI Failed' was a STALE HEAD READ, not a failure: ci-debug status showed the pipeline pending, and the re-run passed and merged."  # a1fe
